<article class="env-definition" id="0821">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0821">Definition <span data-tag="0821">67.48.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $\mathcal{A}$ be a quasi-coherent sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-algebras. The <em>integral closure of $\mathcal{O}_ X$ in $\mathcal{A}$</em> is the quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-subalgebra $\mathcal{A}' \subset \mathcal{A}$ constructed in Lemma <a href="/tag/0820" data-tag="0820">67.48.1</a> above. </p>
</article>